n February 16, 1970, Boston, Massachusetts.\nIn 1988, he started as a DJ in Boston's club \"Loft\". His first release followed in 1992. In 1994, he reached the Dance charts for the first time with his single \"[url=https://www.discogs.com/master/76578-Armand-Van-Helden-Witch-Doktor]Witch Doktor[/url]\".\nHis commercial breakthrough followed in 1996 with a remix of [a9902]' song \"[url=https://www.discogs.com/master/65109-Tori-Amos-Professional-Widow]Professional Widow[/url]\", which reached number one in UK.\nIn the following years, Van Helden had success in both, remixing other artists and as releasing artist. He remixed songs for e.g. [a20991] and [a8024].\nWith his own work, he reached the top of the UK charts for the first time in 1999, when his single \"[url=https://www.discogs.com/master/76593-Armand-Van-Helden-Feat-Duane-Harden-You-Dont-Know-Me]You Don't Know Me[/url]\" reached the peak position. His success continued in the 2000's and in 2010, when he had worldwide success with his project [a224797], he reached multiple peak positions in Europe with the single \"[url=https://www.discogs.com/master/284057-Duck-Sauce-Barbra-Streisand]Barbara Streisand[/url]\".\nHe founded his own label [l=Armed Records] in 1998, and [l=Stupid Fresh] in 2002.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3352","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":7305,"name":"Hardhead"},{"id":13138,"name":"Deep Creed"},{"id":20932,"name":"The Mole People"},{"id":34321,"name":"Circle Children"},{"id":43478,"name":"Buddha Baboons"},{"id":58216,"name":"Sultans Of Swing"},{"id":59063,"name":"Chupacabra"},{"id":64818,"name":"Wizzard Of Wax"},{"id":64824,"name":"Armand & The Banana Spliffs"},{"id":65484,"name":"Jungle Juice"},{"id":97808,"name":"Pirates Of The Caribbean"},{"id":142885,"name":"Old School Junkies"},{"id":304870,"name":"Banji Boys (2)"},{"id":2132282,"name":"Armand Van Haagen Das"}],"groups":[{"active":true,"id":4371,"name":"Subspecies"},{"active":true,"id":4372,"name":"Da Mongoloids"},{"active"